BAO PATCH bao-0003 — JS_IsProxy (fork patch, REQ-ENG-007 U7)
Source: authored in the patched vendor tree (vendor/mozjs/src-js/mozjs/js/src/{jsapi.cpp,jsapi.h}).
Upstream base: jsapi.h side applies on pristine mozjs-153.3.0 (global-scope extern, immediately
  after the JS_NewEmulatesUndefinedFunction declaration — same anchor region as bao-0002).
Semantics: exact proxy internal-slot probe for node:util types.isProxy oracle parity. js::IsProxy
  is a public inline in js/public/Proxy.h (shape->isProxy()) with no C-linkage of its own; this
  thin JS_PUBLIC_API wrapper gives the embedder a linkable entry point. Function proxies
  (typeof "function") and object proxies both answer true; non-proxy objects (incl. functions)
  answer false. Replaces the retired structured-clone heuristic which could not detect function
  proxies (bao U7 leak-face probe: node v24 100% detection vs bao false-negative).
CAUTION (link-name trap, same as bao-0002): the jsapi.h declaration must stay at GLOBAL scope —
  moving it inside namespace JS makes bindgen emit a JS::-prefixed mangled link_name that no
  longer matches the C++ definition -> link failure. Do not "tidy" it into the namespace.
The Rust binding side lives in mozjs/src/jsapi2_wrappers.in.rs (bao git tracked; wrap! next to
  JS_NewEmulatesUndefinedFunction) and is NOT part of this patch. No bindgen blacklist entry is
  involved: bindgen generates the extern declaration from jsapi.h automatically, and the wrap!
  macro in wrappers2 emits the Handle-typed inline wrapper around it.
Replay: paths are SM-tree-relative (-p1); applied after bao-0002 (bao- prefix sorts last).
  Validate: git apply --check --directory=<SM tree> <this file>.

diff --git a/js/src/jsapi.cpp b/js/src/jsapi.cpp
--- a/js/src/jsapi.cpp
+++ b/js/src/jsapi.cpp
@@ -2418,6 +2418,16 @@
   return obj;
 }

+JS_PUBLIC_API bool JS_IsProxy(JSObject* obj) {
+  // Bao extension (REQ-ENG-007, U7): thin linkable wrapper over the public
+  // inline js::IsProxy (js/public/Proxy.h). Exact internal-slot probe
+  // mirroring node:util types.isProxy — function proxies (typeof "function")
+  // and object proxies both answer true, no structured-clone heuristic.
+  return obj && js::IsProxy(obj);
+}
+
 JS_PUBLIC_API JSFunction* JS::GetSelfHostedFunction(JSContext* cx,
                                                     const char* selfHostedName,
                                                     HandleId id,
